Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(engine): host AI controllers in MatchHost + expose
 match outcome (M8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MatchHost gains optional AI controllers (MatchHost::with_controllers),
a command log (MatchHost::log — the same shape as AiMatchHost::log, the
record of every fed command including rejections), and the match outcome
(MatchHost::outcome / MatchHost::is_finished — stage 10's MatchEnded
surfaces through the boundary). The M3 exit criterion holds: the Sim is
still private, submit + advance are still the only mutation paths, and
controllers receive an immutable PlayerView (FD-7) — they never see
&mut Sim. The windowed client will host its vs-AI opponent through this
same seam (A-063 extended to the client — the plan's hosting loop is
one loop, shared with the tools and tests).

Clone/Debug derives removed — Box<dyn Controller> carries neither, and
no caller clones a MatchHost (the M3 tests assert on outcomes, not on
the host). Restart is by drop + reconstruct (the client retains its
ContentBundle and MatchSetup; A15 constructs two fresh MatchHost
instances) — avoids the controller-state-reset problem cleanly.

3 engine unit tests pin the new behavior: a controller runs on the tick
boundary and its command is logged; match outcome surfaces through the
host (the M3 test world has no Footprint kinds so the A-067 guard keeps
the match ongoing — the M8 acceptance test drives a structure-bearing
world); fresh construction with the same seed produces identical hashes
(A15 restart cleanliness). 312/312 dev tests green.
