MatchSummary gains a `winner: Option<PlayerId>` field, populated from
stage 10's MatchEnded event. The headless runner keeps running its tick
budget regardless of whether the match resolves — the M7 "matches
complete" contract is "ran the budget under the A12 checker without
crashing", not "the match resolved". The CLI prints one of three
outcomes: a player wins, mutual destruction (NEUTRAL), or unresolved
(ran the budget).

The scripted Alpha vs Alpha match at the flagship budget (seed 7, 7200
ticks) does not resolve — the opponent isn't aggressive enough to
eliminate the other's command center in four minutes (the plan notes
the Alpha is a scripted opponent, not an evaluative one). The new tools
test asserts the field exists structurally and that the M7 golden
contract holds (241 checkpoints, final hash 0x679f4713114765c9). The
forced-defeat scenario belongs in tests/match_rules.rs.

11/11 tools tests green (was 10, +1 new).
