The windowed client hosts its vs-AI opponent through MatchHost::with_controllers
(A-063: the engine's hosting loop is one loop, shared with the tools and
tests). A fresh ScriptedController is constructed at startup and on every
restart from the same bundle + seed, so a same-seed restart reproduces the
same match bit-for-bit (A15).

UI depth (plan §11.3 / §11.4 / §14 M8):
- End screen: when host.is_finished(), an overlay panel renders VICTORY /
  DEFEAT / MUTUAL DESTRUCTION with a '[R] restart    [Esc] quit' hint.
- Restart: 'R' drops the host and constructs a fresh one (fresh controller,
  fresh Sim, fresh clock, cleared selection + control groups + counters).
- Control groups 1-9: Ctrl+digit assigns the current selection; digit alone
  recalls it (the snapshot filters dead ids — ids are never reused, so a
  stale group reference is harmless).
- Hotkeys: 'S' issues Stop on the selection; 'A' issues AttackMove at the
  cursor (combat semantics from M6). Both fire only while the match is
  ongoing (end-screen 'R' takes over when finished).

The host keeps advancing past MatchEnded (the sim keeps stepping for replay
fidelity); the client's match loop continues to render the world, with the
end-screen panel layered on top. The headless smoke path is unchanged
(MatchHost::new, no controllers) — it tests the engine path, not the AI.

312/312 dev tests green; the M7 goldens (0x9d5ba9b565060336 demo,
0x679f4713114765c9 AI-vs-AI flagship) and the content hash
(0x249b69f0ee343a10) are unchanged.
