tests/match_rules.rs (7 tests) pins the M8 behaviors:

- resignation_ends_the_match_with_the_other_player_winning — a controller
  that resigns on tick 0 drives MatchEnded through the host; the other
  player wins.
- match_ended_fires_exactly_once_even_after_more_ticks — the outcome cache
  is the idempotency guarantee (stage 10 never re-emits).
- the_human_resigning_ends_the_match_with_the_ai_winning — the mirror: the
  human's submitted Resign command ends the match with the AI winning.
- a15_two_fresh_hosts_produce_identical_state_hashes — two MatchHost
  instances from the same setup produce identical hashes at every step
  (plan §9.7, A15).
- a15_two_fresh_hosts_with_ai_produce_identical_logs_and_hashes — the
  stricter A15: with AI controllers, the deterministic controller RNG
  (seeded from the match seed) makes the command logs identical too. A
  same-seed restart reproduces the same match bit-for-bit.
- stage_10_does_not_change_the_m7_golden_checkpoint_trail — the M7 flagship
  golden (0x679f4713114765c9 at seed 7 / 7200 ticks) holds with stage 10
  active. The M8 invariant: match rules land without breaking a single
  M7 golden (A-066: the outcome is derived, not hashed).
- a_resolved_match_surfaces_match_ended_in_the_event_stream — the
  MatchEnded event flows through FrameOutcome.events (FD-9: events flow
  outward), so the client's event consumer sees it for the end-screen
  trigger.

